WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.100
Good morning John. Thanks for your video this week,

00:00:02.180 --> 00:00:04.220
uh it has been really hard,

00:00:04.220 --> 00:00:07.800
impossible, maybe, to think much about policy this election season

00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:10.320
but the really significant interest in that video, uh,

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:13.780
was encouraging, because it means that people do still care about policy,

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:17.020
even if it seems like it's all about personality and storytelling

00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:18.520
and demonizing the other.

00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:21.360
But, with that said, I'm now going to go in the other direction.

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:22.100
I apologize.

00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:25.000
and talk a little bit about the ideas and the stories

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:28.240
that are behind not just politics in the US right now

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:30.400
but I think politics all over the place.

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:34.580
There has been a rise in nationalism and protectionism.

00:00:34.580 --> 00:00:38.400
And the story those people are telling is often about  how awful things are.

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:41.160
About the great coming wave of our enemies,

00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:44.200
about how we have let ourselves be corrupted,

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:49.160
and worst, about how we've consciously decided to be weak.

00:00:49.160 --> 00:00:52.460
I don't even know what to call this ideology, it probably has some name that I don't know,

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:55.760
but at its heart, I feel like there's a perspective that I cannot abide:

00:00:55.760 --> 00:00:57.800
that strength is control,

00:00:57.800 --> 00:01:00.040
and that compassion is weakness.

00:01:00.040 --> 00:01:03.020
I can understand how and why this misconception occurs,

00:01:03.020 --> 00:01:06.440
if you're strong, you can make the world how you want it to be.

00:01:06.460 --> 00:01:09.100
And many want to change how the world is -

00:01:09.100 --> 00:01:11.440
maybe they need to change how the world is.

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:15.300
They have legitimate insecurities for themselves and their families.

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:17.900
But to go beyond that, in your rhetoric as a politician,

00:01:17.900 --> 00:01:19.980
into "this country is losing",

00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:25.320
rather than we need to use the resources we have, and there are many, to protect our citizens?

00:01:25.720 --> 00:01:28.160
That's not about protecting anyone.

00:01:28.160 --> 00:01:33.040
To me, it feels like trying to find people's wounds, their insecurities, and their biases,

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:35.840
and then aggravating those wounds intentionally.

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:39.340
Part of the secret to this rhetoric is that you can never call the country strong,

00:01:39.340 --> 00:01:40.460
that would be counter-productive.

00:01:40.460 --> 00:01:44.240
We can't talk about the fact that American industrial production is higher now than it has ever been,

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:45.460
that the job market is strong,

00:01:45.460 --> 00:01:49.700
that the American military spends more than the next eight militaries combined.

00:01:49.700 --> 00:01:54.780
This rhetoric is based on inflaming or manufacturing fear and insecurity.

00:01:54.780 --> 00:02:00.200
Because from there comes ruthlessness, comes disregard for morality, comes self-righteousness,

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:04.900
comes the framing of people who are not like us as either evil or corrupt,

00:02:04.900 --> 00:02:08.400
whether that's Syrians, or protesters, or political opponents.

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:13.560
It can be part of our job, as citizens of a democracy, to recognize when the fears being pitched to us

00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:15.340
are made of cardboard and styrofoam.

00:02:15.380 --> 00:02:18.240
Because yes, we do have huge problems to face.

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:24.220
Problems old and new that can be influenced by good policy and good people and good strategy.

00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:27.540
But so much of the fear we have been fed

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:29.820
is no more real than a Transformers movie.

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:32.400
They have to say our country is losing

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:38.300
because a country that is strong digs deep not into building walls and dehumanizing other people,

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:40.860
but into civic service, and altruism,

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:44.180
into openness, and understanding, and peacekeeping, and collaboration.

00:02:44.180 --> 00:02:47.620
Just as when an individual person is confident and self-assured,

00:02:47.620 --> 00:02:52.800
the only logical course is to try and share that great gift that you have been given with other people.

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:55.900
Compassion is the ultimate manifestation of strength.

00:02:55.900 --> 00:02:59.100
And because America is strong, our compassion has grown.

00:02:59.100 --> 00:03:02.920
We have finally opened up the joy of marriage to all loving couples,

00:03:02.920 --> 00:03:05.280
we have opened the doors to immigrants and refugees,

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:08.400
We are finally taking a look at some of our traditions and language

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:10.500
and recognizing the hurt that they can cause,

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:13.380
and many are open to conversations about mass incarceration

00:03:13.380 --> 00:03:16.800
and how it has disproportionately affected people of color.

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:18.740
And of course we have a long way yet to go.

00:03:18.740 --> 00:03:22.240
But to those who see that progress as a manifestation of weakness,

00:03:22.240 --> 00:03:26.640
to the people who puff themselves up, and beat their chests, and yell about strength

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:29.860
while pouring salt into the wounds of insecurity and fear,

00:03:30.040 --> 00:03:35.160
I can never see your rhetoric as anything other than sad, hurtful weakness.

00:03:35.160 --> 00:03:41.500
Weakness that is getting in the way of our  ability  to get on doing the good work that humanity needs to do.

00:03:41.500 --> 00:03:45.540
And I have no doubt that in the fullness of time we will move past this,

00:03:45.540 --> 00:03:47.620
and we will do that good work.

00:03:47.620 --> 00:03:49.600
John, I'll see you on Tuesday.

